      "source": "The following example shows how to compress data from a string and prints the sizes of the data instances to illustrate the amount of compression:",
      "normalizedSource": "The following example shows how to compress data from a string and prints the sizes of the data instances to illustrate the amount of compression:",
      "sourceHash": "7b577b99e22c880acc1893dd60cce88a9f0928441c83f2d0286f5cf37e7eb8eb",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "If your data object is already in a compressed format, such as media formats like JPEG images or AAC audio, [`compress(using:)`](nsmutabledata/compress(using:).md) may provide minimal or no benefit.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nvar string = \"NSData and its mutable subclass NSMutableData provide data objects, or object-oriented wrappers for byte buffers. Data objects let simple allocated buffers (that is, data with no embedded pointers) take on the behavior of Foundation objects.\"\nlet data = NSMutableData(data: Data(string.utf8))\nprint (\"original data size: \\(data.length)\")\ndo {\n    try data.compress(using: .zlib)\n    print(\"zlib compressed size: \\(data.length)\")\n} catch {\n    print (\"Compression error: \\(error)\")\n}\n// Prints:\n//  original data size: 241\n//  zlib compressed size: 158\n```",
      "documentTitle": "compress(using:)",
