      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "code:discussion:0010",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nvar string = \"NSData and its mutable subclass NSMutableData provide data objects, or object-oriented wrappers for byte buffers. Data objects let simple allocated buffers (that is, data with no embedded pointers) take on the behavior of Foundation objects.\"\nlet data = NSMutableData(data: Data(string.utf8))\nprint (\"original data size: \\(data.length)\")\ndo {\n    try data.compress(using: .zlib)\n    print(\"zlib compressed size: \\(data.length)\")\n} catch {\n    print (\"Compression error: \\(error)\")\n}\n// Prints:\n//  original data size: 241\n//  zlib compressed size: 158\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift var string = \"NSData and its mutable subclass NSMutableData provide data objects, or object-oriented wrappers for byte buffers. Data objects let simple allocated buffers (that is, data with no embedded pointers) take on the behavior of Foundation objects.\" let data = NSMutableData(data: Data(string.utf8)) print (\"original data size: \\(data.length)\") do { try data.compress(using: .zlib) print(\"zlib compressed size: \\(data.length)\") } catch { print (\"Compression error: \\(error)\") } // Prints: // original data size: 241 // zlib compressed size: 158 ```",
      "sourceHash": "aa7e5258d94df9ee1df26b2f9ef069aa407d79593bfd4afd847e1cec7c0e37ba",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
